==Trivia==
*''Nova'' is an astronomical term for a star that suddenly becomes much brighter and then returns to its original luminosity over a period of time. ''Nova'' is also the feminine form of the Latin word ''novus'', meaning "new".
*She may be based on various plant-related mythical humanoids such as the [[wikipedia:Dryad|dryad]], [[wikipedia:Hamadryad|hamadryad]] and [https://www.dandwiki.com/wiki/Alraune_(5e_Race) alraune].
*Her Evolved Form's headpiece looks similar to that of [[wikia:darksouls:Dark Sun Gwyndolin|Dark Sun Gwyndolin]], a boss from the game ''Dark Souls''.
*She may be the ancient god from the [[Uncanny Legends]] ending, as she appears in [[Sacred Forest]] and [[Sage of Life Dr. Nova]]'s Japanese description states that she guided the Cat Army to another dimension, while the Uncanny Legends ending states that an ancient god appeared from a golden tree and told the Cat Army to find a [[:Category:Sage Enemies|Sage]] in another world.
*She is the first Cat Unit to have the [[Explosion]] ability.
*The line "a world where Cats are at work or at school" in Dr. Nova's Japanese description references the [[Empire of Cats]] ending.
*Prior to [[Version 14.0 Update|Version 14.0]], both of Master of Life Dr. Nova's forms had a minimum spawn layer of 5 rather than 0.
*Dr. Nova is the only Sage Mythic Cat without the conjure ability.

